<title>BOTSWANA: RDC Properties year share rises.</title>
<headline>RDC Properties year share rises.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31 1996</p>
<p>			(million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)		     21.4 vs   19.1</p>
<p>Total dividend</p>
<p>	per linked unit (thebe)  0.30  vs   13.00</p>
<p>Total interest</p>
<p>	per linked unit (thebe) 15.90 vs	nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			 5.227 vs    4.836</p>
<p>    Debenture interest	  1.352 vs    1.213</p>
<p>    Taxation			  nil vs    0.303</p>
<p>    Turnover			8.349 vs    7.023</p>
<p>Second half dividend and interest payable May 30, 1997</p>
<p>To linked unitholders registered at the close of business on 23 May, 1997.</p>
<p>Full name: Realestate Development Properties Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - Due to the restructure of the group as a variable loan stock company the comparative data is pro-forma as contained in the circular to shareholders dated 7 August 996.</p>
<p>In a statement the directors said the market had reacted positively to the restructuring and that the capital raised and linked units issued had enabled the company to acquire 100 percent interests in two prime properties which would contribute to a substantial increase in future rental income of the company.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
